Until recently I played NetHack 3.1 on a 16 Mhz 286 machine with 2 Meg
of memory.  I had freed up as much of the lower 640K as I could and had
defined most of the 1-2Meg range as disk cache.  With that configuration
I was able to get reasonable performace, though it got sluggish at times,
especially on levels with a lot of monsters (e.g. Fort Ludios).

